# {{ .Name }} ({{ .Type | title }})

Get information on a notification resource, including which system events it is configured to
alert on and where those alerts are sent.

## Example Usage

```terraform
# Get information about a specific notification
data "wallix-bastion_notification" "storage_alerts" {
  notification_name = "storage-alerts"
}

# Reuse its destination when creating a related notification
resource "wallix-bastion_notification" "storage_alerts_secondary" {
  notification_name = "storage-alerts-secondary"
  description       = "Secondary alert channel mirroring ${data.wallix-bastion_notification.storage_alerts.notification_name}"
  enabled           = data.wallix-bastion_notification.storage_alerts.enabled
  type              = data.wallix-bastion_notification.storage_alerts.type
  destination       = data.wallix-bastion_notification.storage_alerts.destination
  language          = data.wallix-bastion_notification.storage_alerts.language
  events            = data.wallix-bastion_notification.storage_alerts.events
}

# Check whether a specific event is monitored
output "monitors_disk_space" {
  value = contains(data.wallix-bastion_notification.storage_alerts.events, "disk_space_critical")
}
```

{{ .SchemaMarkdown | trimspace }}

## Usage Notes

### `notification_name`

The Required lookup key. It must match an existing notification exactly; the data source fails
with an error if no notification with that name exists.

### `destination`

For the only currently supported `type` (`email`), this is a list of recipient email addresses
separated by `;`.

### `events`

The full set of system events currently configured to trigger this notification. Order is not
significant since this is a set.
